        "original_id": "09744db2-efc2-5d56-abcc-372f75c7698c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: New York Islanders, New York Rangers, Pittsburgh Penguins, New Jersey Devils, WWE\n- Places: Madison Square Garden, New York City, New York metropolitan area\n- Events: 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, Survivor Series (2011)\n- Topics: NHL franchises, arena tenants\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders defeated the New York Rangers in three games in the first round.\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders defeated the Pittsburgh Penguins in seven games in the Quarter-finals after losing the first three games.\n- Madison Square Garden has been the home of the New York Rangers of the NHL and the New York Knicks of the NBA, and since 1997 it has also been home to the New York Liberty of the WNBA.\n- Survivor Series (2011) was a WWE professional wrestling pay-per-view event held on November 20, 2011 at Madison Square Garden in New York City.\n- The New York Rangers are one of three NHL franchises in the New York metropolitan area, along with the New Jersey Devils and the New York Islanders.",
